## Priority order

Ranked by impact on the promise, weighted by evidence the gap is real and by
implementation cost.

| # | Change | Gap | Effort | Why now |
|---|--------|-----|--------|---------|
| 1 | Log what actually matters (business outcomes + the discarded OCR fields) | §1 | S | Prerequisite for everything below. Data is already being thrown away. |
| 2 | Weekly Scorecard — grade last week's bet, show it Monday | §2 | M | Highest-value retention surface; makes the strategist promise real. |
| 3 | Skip-reason loop + server-side posted state | §4 | S | Attacks execution rate, which multiplies every other gain. |
| 4 | Dimension the results learning (pillar / funnel stage / hook archetype) | §3 | S-M | Turns analytics into insight a creator can't self-diagnose. |
| 5 | Post-stream voice repair on Plan + read thumbs-up back into generation | §5, §6 | M | Core promise on the core surface; currently measured and ignored. |
| 6 | Durable, visible, editable Voice Profile | §6 | M-L | The only real switching cost, and the answer to "why month six." |
| 7 | Monthly "what changed in the algorithm" note | §7 | S | Credits work the product already does and pays for. |

Items 1–4 are, together, roughly one focused cycle, and they convert the product
from "generates content" to "shows you what worked and why." That is the whole
argument.

